cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use dynG in your work, please cite the software as below, and also the paper
  behind each algorithm you use (listed under references; see the README table).
type: software
title: "dynG: dynamic graph and hypergraph updates on GPUs"
abstract: >-
  dynG is a C++17/CUDA library (Python bindings planned) that keeps the results of graph
  and hypergraph algorithms up to date while the structure changes in batches, without
  recomputing from scratch. It unifies the research codes of DynaMOSP, DynLP,
  ESCHER/ESCHER+, H-SOSP and TruCy/DynTruCy.
authors:
  - family-names: Shovan
    given-names: S M
    affiliation: Missouri University of Science and Technology
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dyng-dev/dyng"
url: "https://github.com/dyng-dev/dyng"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - dynamic graph
  - batch update
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - hypergraph
  - shortest paths
  - cycle counting
  - triad counting
  - label propagation
